# The MLP replaced by its best affine approximation

Generated by `mlp_affine.py` (exploratory). Affine maps fitted by ridge on LN(mid) → MLP output at every live token of the fit episodes under every goal (shared: one map; per-goal: one map per goal; constant: the mean output; 'in the residual': fitted on mid, the layer norm removed too). Behaviour: greedy return on the test spawns (the natural model 0.548, QMDP 0.551, goal-blind H policy as the floor of the recovery); agreement with the natural model's own-goal decisions on its test decisions (all, and those where its move depends on the goal); the share of decisions whose move depends on the goal. Transport at the input of block 2 (equiv2's recipe, refitted on the variant's states): held-out R² of the ridge map M(A→B) between goals' difference vectors; on the A-equivalent, B-different pairs, B's decision switched to the donor's by the direct B-written difference, by M(A→B) Δ_A, by Δ_A and by random. Medians (min–max) over six models.

